From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] configfile: let ad5x_plugins write the plugin list before a
 config read

Kiln OS only. ad5x.cfg includes plugins-active.cfg, the printer's
plugins.cfg with each enabled plugin that can't run (incompatible,
broken, missing, a required plugin off, a conflict) left out, so a
skipped plugin's config isn't read. Klipper offers no step before it
reads its config, so read_main_config calls
extras.ad5x_plugins.before_config_read() first: the list follows
plugins.cfg at every start, RESTART and FIRMWARE_RESTART, also when the
last start stopped before [ad5x_plugins]. Without that module (a plain
Klipper) nothing changes; an error there is logged, never fatal.
---
 klippy/configfile.py | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/klippy/configfile.py b/klippy/configfile.py
--- a/klippy/configfile.py
+++ b/klippy/configfile.py
@@ -477,6 +477,14 @@
         fileconfig = cfgrdr.build_fileconfig(data, filename)
         return ConfigWrapper(self.printer, fileconfig, {}, 'printer')
     def read_main_config(self):
+        # Kiln OS: [ad5x_plugins] writes the plugin include list
+        # (plugins-active.cfg) from plugins.cfg first, so an edit of
+        # plugins.cfg applies at the next start or RESTART
+        try:
+            import extras.ad5x_plugins
+            extras.ad5x_plugins.before_config_read(self.printer)
+        except Exception:
+            logging.exception("ad5x_plugins: plugin list not updated")
         fileconfig, autosave_fileconfig = self.autosave.load_main_config()
         access_tracking = self.validate.start_access_tracking(
             autosave_fileconfig)
